//! Raw FFI bindings to the handful of libraw_r C functions/types this crate
//! calls, generated by build.rs via bindgen. See raw_decode.rs for the safe
//! wrapper -- nothing outside that module should touch this directly.
//!
//! Why hand-bind this instead of using an existing crate (checked
//! 2026-11-26, worth re-checking if revisiting this): the pure-Rust
//! `rawler` crate's public API only exposes full demosaic decode via
//! `decode_file`/`decode`, with no "give me the default-processed preview"
//! step -- exactly the thing LibRaw's `dcraw_process` is good at. The
//! published Rust LibRaw bindings are either abandoned (`libraw-sys`, last
//! published 2015, almost certainly ABI-stale against a modern LibRaw) or
//! early-stage/"passively maintained" (`libraw-rs`) with no documented
//! `dcraw_process`/`dcraw_make_mem_image` coverage. Binding directly to the
//! handful of C functions actually needed, via bindgen against the
//! system's `libraw_r`, was more reliable than depending on either.
#![allow(
    non_camel_case_types,
    non_snake_case,
    non_upper_case_globals,
    dead_code
)]

include!(concat!(env!("OUT_DIR"), "/libraw_bindings.rs"));
